<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#1a1b1f">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}<link rel="icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 96 }}">{%- endif -%}
  <title>{{ page_title }}{% unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless %}</title>
  {%- if page_description -%}<meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">{%- endif -%}

  {{ content_for_header }}

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'xero-theme.css' | asset_url }}">
  {%- comment -%} Overrides only, must load after xero-theme.css. {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'xero-fix.css' | asset_url }}">
  {%- comment -%}
    The segmented control (3D/Photos, Day/Night, Studio/City/Mars). Its own file because it
    is one component with a long rationale, and because its geometry and colour logic must
    have exactly one home - the whole class of bugs there came from the same relationship
    being asserted in several places at once. Must load after xero-fix.css.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'xero-pill.css' | asset_url }}">

  {%- comment -%}
    xero-stage.js resolves three and three/addons/ with bare specifiers inside its dynamic
    import(), so the page needs an import map for the GLB path to work at all. It must be
    parsed before the first dynamic import runs, hence head. The DRACO decoder path inside
    stage.js is pinned to the same version.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    SELF-HOSTED three.js, bundled INTO THE THEME (assets/). Previously loaded from unpkg.com
    (third-party CDN) which was slow/blocked on mobile so the 3D bike never appeared. Now the
    four modules ship inside the theme itself and load via asset_url from whatever store the
    theme is installed on - so the theme is portable to any account and depends on NO external
    CDN. Minified build = ~half the size. GLTFLoader's one relative import was rewired to the
    bare 'three/addons/utils/...' specifier so it resolves through this map.
    (Not in {% raw %}: the URLs come from asset_url, which needs Liquid.)
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="importmap">
  {
    "imports": {
      "three": "{{ 'three.module.min.js' | asset_url }}",
      "three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js": "{{ 'GLTFLoader.js' | asset_url }}",
      "three/addons/loaders/DRACOLoader.js": "{{ 'DRACOLoader.js' | asset_url }}",
      "three/addons/utils/BufferGeometryUtils.js": "{{ 'BufferGeometryUtils.js' | asset_url }}"
    }
  }
  </script>

  <script>
    /* Shopify serves assets from its CDN, so every path must come from Liquid.
       The stage can never build one by string concatenation. */
    /* Only City and Mars are photographic. Studio is drawn as geometry by the stage and
       has no image files, so including it here produced empty asset_url strings. */
    window.XERO_ASSETS = {
      worlds: {
        {%- assign panos = 'city-day,city-night,mars-day,mars-night' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- for p in panos -%}
          "{{ p }}": {
            "1600": "{{ p | append: '-1600.webp' | asset_url }}",
            "900":  "{{ p | append: '-900.webp'  | asset_url }}"
          }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
        {%- endfor -%}
      },
      bikeDay:   "{{ 'bike-day.webp'   | asset_url }}",
      bikeNight: "{{ 'bike-night.webp' | asset_url }}",
      bikeSeam:  "{{ 'bike-seam.webp'  | asset_url }}"
    };
    window.XERO_ROUTES = {
      cartAdd:    "{{ routes.cart_add_url }}.js",
      cartChange: "{{ routes.cart_change_url }}.js",
      cart:       "{{ routes.cart_url }}.js",
      checkout:   "{{ routes.cart_url }}/checkout"
    };
    window.XERO_MONEY_FORMAT = {{ shop.money_format | json }};
    window.XERO_SETTINGS = {
      splash:   false,
      splashMs: 0
    };
  </script>

  <script src="{{ 'xero-stage.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
  <script src="{{ 'xero-store.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
  {%- comment -%}
    Mounts the GLB and replaces the stage's limited sprite arc with a real turntable.
    Must load after both of the above: it patches objects they create.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script src="{{ 'xero-model.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
</head>

<body>
  {%- section 'xero-header' -%}

  <main id="MainContent">
    {{ content_for_layout }}
  </main>

  {%- comment -%}
    Persistent chrome: mini bar, sticky cart, cart drawer, intro screen.
    Rendered outside {{ content_for_layout }} so it survives navigation.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- section 'xero-chrome' -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    THE MODEL.

    Inline body scripts run before deferred scripts, so this wins over anything a section
    set earlier in the page.

    XERO_MODEL_URL - Shopify transcoded the product's Model3d into a 5.8 MB plain GLB on
    its CDN, 20x lighter than the raw upload and needing no special decoders. Swap this URL
    if the model itself is ever replaced.

    XERO_TEXTURE_URL - the EDITED skin atlas. The GLB carries its colour atlas in the
    emissive slot; this is an edited version of that exact atlas, painted over the same UV
    layout, and xero-model.js's retexture() rebinds it onto the model's emissiveMap at
    runtime. So a new skin is one file upload here, not a GLB re-export. Set this back to ""
    to fall back to the map baked into the GLB. Change the ?v= when you replace the file -
    it is the cache key.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    /* GLB stays a CDN URL: Shopify does NOT allow .glb as a theme asset, so the 3D model
       cannot travel inside the theme. On a NEW account, re-upload the GLB to that store's
       Content > Files (or the product's 3D media) and paste its URL here. This URL is public
       and will keep working as long as the original store's files exist. */
    window.XERO_MODEL_URL = "https://cdn.shopify.com/3d/models/o/ffa775409b18ef79/XERO_Chiron.glb";
    /* Final edited skin - now bundled INTO THE THEME (assets/), so it is portable and needs
       no external CDN. Set to "" to fall back to the GLB's own baked map. */
    window.XERO_TEXTURE_URL = "{{ 'xero-skin-final.jpg' | asset_url }}";
  </script>
</body>
</html>
